      "prompt": "Design an original ECLIPSE action RPG A1 ASHEN APPROACH ultrawide 3:1 2D side-scrolling BACK scenery plate, native fine clustered pixel art circa 420 by 140. Attached picture is the NEXT level; match ONLY its dusky lavender light, deep smoky ink-blue palette, delicate dither, ragged silhouette shapes and edge detail. The geography here must be entirely different: this is the OPEN ROAD long BEFORE the gate. Sky freely visible above the traveler, low sweeping causeway through ash-covered moor, spacious blue-violet sky with long streaks of storm cloud and bright lavender light low in gaps on the horizon. An imposing, wind-bent, near-black torn military standard in left third, its faded overlapping-disc motif and trailing cloth point right; a line of half-buried broken boundary markers follows the long low road, foreground slate debris, thinner silhouettes in middle distance. An extremely faint SMALL fragment of distant outer fortress WALL at x70–83% width is the sole architectural hint of destination. NO doors, gates, archways, towers, castles on a hill, hallways, ceilings, bridge arcades, or characters. No UI, no text. Keep all tall objects off-center. Bottom 15% is simple dark ashen earth (playable stone lip overlaid separately). Looming march into danger. Purple light showing between torn cloth, ruined pikes, stone fragments, reeds; high contrast ground silhouettes. Detailed pixel sprites background, not realistic painted landscape, not cute. Three engaging horizontal fields for side-scrolling.",
