      "prompt": "Paint a major architecture replacement on the RIGHT HALF of this exact panoramic side-scroller background. The owner specifically rejects refined, slick, elegant carved masonry. Remove the existing spear buttresses and smooth giant stone facets completely. Rebuild the gatehouse as a battered, hulking fieldstone keep with an ugly stubborn weight: huge rough-hewn uneven blocks interlocked with little chocking stones; visibly projecting blunt stones next to sunken stones; deep black uneven joints, thick rubble-filled core showing through a bite torn from its shoulder. Big structural silhouette changes, not surface noise. Thick squat square pier and a mismatched roundish crumbling pier, broad flat-topped battered parapet, NO pointed buttresses, no sharp fins, bevels or needle caps. One thick splintered dark timber lintel with crude black iron dogs, the open beaten iron gate below, weathered simple eclipse maker's mark incised small. Use clustered near-black shadows and sparse lavender light on the ragged upper lips of individual blocks. Readable large stone clusters at 432x144. Avoid noisy gravel texture everywhere. Sweeping violet sky, A1 road, left milestone, original human-scale doorway opening center about x87%, floor y87%, and 3:1 landscape framing stay consistent. Road into gate, no obstructions, no overhead suspended objects, no humans or UI. Authentic chunky dark pixel game environment, foreboding and timeworn. This should read as a thick fortress built stone by stone even from a distance.",
